%description:
DcTcp with SACK recovers as TcpReno does: in the fast recovery,
Rfc6675Recovery takes each ACK of new data, and cwnd does not grow. The
tester drops every second segment from a20 to a34, so the recovery gets
seven partial ACKs. The recovery ends at B036 with cwnd at ssthresh, 9216.
The next four ACKs grow cwnd in congestion avoidance to 9661, so nine
segments go out at t=1.029 s. Before, DcTcp grew cwnd at each partial ACK
after the first and at the ACK that ended the recovery, to 10393 after
B040, and sent ten segments. The trace is the same as with TcpReno and
TcpNewReno.
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true

*.tcptester.cmdenv-log-level=DEBUG
**.cmdenv-log-level=OFF

*.cli_app.tSend=1s
*.cli_app.sendBytes=65536B # 64 1024-byte segments

*.tcptester.script="a20 delete; a22 delete; a24 delete; a26 delete; a28 delete; a30 delete; a32 delete; a34 delete"  # every second segment of one flight

*.*_tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.*_tcp.advertisedWindow = 65535
*.*_tcp.sackSupport = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%contains: stdout
[1.023 B029] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 19457 win 63487   Option(s): NOP NOP SACK[32769,35841)[30721,31745)[28673,29697)[26625,27649)
[1.023 B030] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 21505 win 61439   Option(s): NOP NOP SACK[32769,35841)[30721,31745)[28673,29697)[26625,27649)
[1.023 B031] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 23553 win 59391   Option(s): NOP NOP SACK[32769,35841)[30721,31745)[28673,29697)[26625,27649)

%contains: stdout
